  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Angola WHO 2025 WASH Lead (cholera)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of early 2025, Angola is facing a serious cholera outbreak - its first since 2018-with over 8,500 confirmed cases and more than 300 deaths reported across 16 provinces. The outbreak is part of a broader resurgence in Southern Africa and is driven by limited access to clean water and sanitation, fragile health infrastructure, seasonal floods, and economic challenges that continue to strain public services. In response, the World Health Organization (WHO) and partners are scaling up emergency efforts and have called for additional technical expertise to support coordination and response activities on the ground. To support on this, the Dutch Disaster Risk Reduction and Surge Support (DRRS) is looking for a water sanitation and hygiene (WASH) lead to work closely with WHO and key partners, supporting the Government of Angola in strengthening and implementing its cholera response efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
